multiScaleR 0.7.11
* Preserve fixed training transformations in native refit, mixed, snapshot,
  raster and curve routes, and recover retained legacy analytic metadata.
* Retain fixed training metadata in returned native Cox fits as well as wrapper predictions.
* Reuse fitted fixed normalization across analytic, prepared, unmarked, and
  admitted conditional-logistic prediction paths, including qualified calls.
* Distinguish fixed logical expressions from actual random-effect declarations
  in prepared response and scale formulas.
* Check public weighted-SQ point, snapshot, and raster predictions against
  independent training transforms and native conditional covariance.
* Qualify native fixed spline metadata without changing native spline methods;
  use the R-recommended splines package only in focused tests.

multiScaleR 0.7.10
* Integrate native formula designs, weighted-SQ prerequisites, and supported
  spatial and step-selection prediction contracts.
* Preserve fitted reference transforms, expanded parameter counts, priors,
  diagnostics, and distinct likelihood and uncertainty targets.
* Add focused compatibility tests and generated documentation; retain private
  fitting restrictions until their numerical and reference gates pass.

Development details
* Keep learned unmarked fixed bases at their training definition across effect
  curves, with native coefficient covariance and inverse links.
* Use active native terms for unmarked curves, distinguishing fixed-expression
  syntax from actual random-effect declarations in plotting metadata.
* Retain formula-offset metadata for native conditional GLM predictions that
  request standard errors.
- Retain native factor products in one-kernel NB2 scale profiles and bootstrap targets; the zero-effect ceiling removes the entire kernel-dependent coefficient block.

* Retain native scalar kernel expressions in analytic and prepared targets,
  with complete derivatives, cold frames, reference units and coefficient priors.

* Retain native product columns in checked analytic raster predictions.
* Support conditional-logistic link and relative-risk projections without
  prediction choice sets, retaining probability and uncertainty safeguards.
* Normalize step-selection choice sets in one registered deterministic native call.

* Connect native response products and factor interactions to joint mixed
  likelihoods and retain raw transform inputs for native effect curves.

* Connect native response products and factor interactions to prepared Bayesian
  targets, proposals, prediction and curves, and private marginal/group/limit
  calculations, preserving reference normalization, priors and admission guards.
* Include expanded response dimensions in conservative AD memory planning.

* Add native R product/factor/crossing designs to analytic GLM/NB2 and
  conditional-logistic fitting, covariance, prediction and snapshots, preserving
  legacy targets and all original numerical gates.
* Reject GAM targets in ordinary analytic GLM adapters instead of discarding
  their smooth bases; native GAM refitting and prediction remain available.
* Preserve quoted predictor names and parse interaction annotations from native
  terms in marginal effect plots.

* Use native Cox event counts for AICc/BIC penalties while retaining all
  alternative rows for comparison, with direct amt wrapper compatibility tests.
* Retain fixed transformations and compound offsets in conditional-logistic
  native refits when an amt fitting call no longer exposes the original data.

* Add private paired spatial scale contrasts from complete joint vectors, with explicit ratio/log-ratio prediction contracts.
* Add private conditional spatial response densities and explicit AIC/BIC admission guards, keeping population and realized latent dimensions separate.
* Add private location-specific spatial scale probability diagnostics using original retained chains, preserving scalar probability rules and public guards.
* Add private spatial-only scale summaries and point maps with frozen reference
  diagnostics, joint uncertainty and explicit calibration limits.

* Add private spatial mean and replicate prediction through shared kernel and
  weighted-SQ validation, preserving frozen fields, joint draws, observation
  noise distinctions and public fitting guards.

* Document and validate private spatial-only scale fields without annual effects,
  preserving fixed normalization, priors and uncertainty distinctions.

* Add a private optimized exact-limit audit component while preserving all original starts, failures, curvature, Poisson and large-SD checks; finite weighted-SQ fitting remains guarded.

* Add ordinary weighted-SQ likelihood evaluation components with independent
  numerical coordinates, preserving fitting admission and uncertainty targets.

* Retain provenance and population dimensions for exact weighted-SQ kernel
  components, with native density and existing AD-constructor compatibility.

* Add explicit whole-model weighted-SQ limiting likelihood components while
  retaining private fitting admission and all numerical safeguards.

* Extend prepared group likelihood limits to supported scale covariates and
