---------
* Strengthen internal weighted-SQ tape admission and exact kernel-limit
  prerequisites while retaining the private likelihood fitting restrictions.
* Native S3 argument abbreviations obey prediction safeguards. Marginal-effect
  intervals are ordered after inverse-link transformation; invalid native
  limits are reported as unavailable without changing fitted values.
* Native lm mean-confidence and future-observation interval columns retain
  their conditional uncertainty targets across points, maps, and snapshots.
  Refit snapshots also preserve compact spaMM variance and interval attributes.
* Real spaMM compatibility now verifies fixed metrics from retained frames,
  supports zero/selected-effect rows, transforms link-scale plot limits, and
  counts all native likelihood parameters. Provider-triggered SEs/covariance
  are identified; raster requests that would lose native covariance fail explicitly.
* Native and raster prediction contracts distinguish returned standard errors
  from point-only outputs and separately recorded snapshot capabilities.
* Refit profile caching has a retained-memory budget and explicit uncached
  operation for oversized payloads or unavailable key storage. Numerical profile
  failures remain errors; cache identity checks and target definitions are retained.
* Partial lme4 predictions require only fixed inputs and selected random-effect
  inputs. Shared contracts retain selected effects and GAM term controls while
  preserving native validation and uncertainty distinctions.

